        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "DEDR 93 lists ಅಟ್ಟ (aṭṭa) beside Tamil aṭṭam, \"terraced roof\", but marks the Kannada word as one of the tatsamas, and notes that it is uncertain whether the word is Indo-Aryan or Dravidian in origin. Sanskrit has aṭṭa, \"tower\" (CDIAL 180), which CDIAL calls non-Aryan."
            }
          ]
        },
